    "state": "present",
    "source": "retro.json",
    "author": "implementer",
    "independent": false,
    "summary": "Repair 4. Fixed the 10 ESLint errors that failed the factory lint stage in server/providers/service-domain.ts and server/providers/service-support.ts, then removed the build blockers the same in-progress feature had left behind: the service-ticket-acceptance Workflow DSL imported three run/condition modules that did not exist and called finalize() on the node-less builder, so the server typecheck and the workflow checker failed. Implemented the missing handlers (is-urgent, register-normal-acceptance, register-urgent-acceptance plus a shared acceptance helper that moves the ticket to pending_process, records the branch note and notifies the assignee idempotently) and finalized the tree that actually holds the node. Also restored the .ts specifiers the source-loaded seed and seed-data require, which had reverted to .js and made tests/logic/app-server.test.ts fail at seed load. Verified: full ESLint clean, pnpm typecheck clean, pnpm nocobase workflow check (3 nodes), all 245 tests, pnpm build (1 workflow artifact) and pnpm nocobase db apply all pass. The business feature layer itself (server routes, client pages, ServiceDomain registration, Scheduler/AI wiring) is still absent and remains the open acceptance gap.",
    "blockers": [],
    "improvements": [
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37453059911/attempt/1/I1",
        "category": "code-quality",
        "title": "`as never` casts hid an inference mismatch instead of a type error",
        "detail": "server/authorization/resources.ts used `as never` in six record-access resolvers and on the composite registration call. The lint rule proved the resolver assertions unnecessary and removing one of them exposed that `define(resource)` could not accept the union of builder types. The runtime intent was already `build()`-based, so the casts were masking an avoidable generic-inference problem.",
        "suggestedChange": "Prefer passing the concrete built value (`resource.build()`) or annotating the collection with the framework's accepted parameter type instead of `as never`.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37453059911/attempt/1/I2",
        "category": "tooling",
        "title": "No guard against .js relative imports from source-loaded seeds and migrations",
        "detail": "server/** may import .js because it runs from compiled dist, but database/** seeds and migrations are dynamically imported from TypeScript source by the app-server task loader, where Node's native type stripping resolves only .ts specifiers. A .js specifier pointing at a .ts file compiles and only fails at application startup with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND.",
        "suggestedChange": "Add a lint or check for relative imports under database/** that requires the .ts extension (or teach the seed/migration loader to resolve .js to .ts) so the mistake fails at author time rather than at runtime.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37453059911/attempt/1/I3",
        "category": "code-quality",
        "title": "A startup registration function existed but had no call site",
        "detail": "server/authorization/resources.ts exported registerServiceAuthorization(), but nothing invoked it. The omission was invisible until seeded grants were validated in AuthorizationProvider.start(), which then failed on every composite action. The declarations were correct; only the lifecycle hook was missing.",
        "suggestedChange": "When a module exports a register*/define* function meant to run at startup, wire it to a named ServiceProvider in the same change, or export the provider instead of a bare function.",
        "mechanizable": false
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37453059911/attempt/1/I4",
        "category": "i18n",
        "title": "A key used by a component but absent from en-US is caught only by a test",
        "detail": "en-US is the source-of-truth locale shape, so zh-CN is typed against AppResource and a missing key there is a compile error. A key present in neither locale, however, compiles and is only caught by tests/logic/app-locale-coverage.test.ts.",
        "suggestedChange": "Optionally type component translation keys against AppResource or add a check that every t() key exists in en-US, so a missing key fails at build time.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37453059911/attempt/1/I5",
        "category": "tooling",
        "title": "Source-loaded database tasks must use .ts specifiers, and the fix regressed",
        "detail": "Repair 2 had fixed database/main/seeds/..._create_service_permission_sets.ts and database/seed-data/permission-sets.ts to import .ts, because seeds and migrations are dynamically imported from TypeScript source (Node type stripping) where a .js specifier pointing at a .ts file throws ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Repair 3 rewrote both back to .js, so the seed-load failure returned in tests/logic/app-server.test.ts. The tsconfigs already allow importing .ts and rewrite it on emit, so the guard below would have caught it.",
        "suggestedChange": "Add a lint/check that relative imports under database/** must use the .ts extension (and the opposite, .js, under server/**), so this recurring mistake fails at author time.",
        "mechanizable": true
      }
    ],
    "note": "实现者自述，未经独立核验；不是框架评审结论。"
  },
